# RTSP Client Request Templates

Based on the DESCRIBE template you provided, here are all the common RTSP client request templates:

## 1. OPTIONS
```
OPTIONS <<URL>> RTSP/1.0\r\n
CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n
User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n
\r\n
```

## 2. DESCRIBE
```
DESCRIBE <<URL>> RTSP/1.0\r\n
CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n
User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Accept: <<VALUE>>\r\n
\r\n
```

## 3. SETUP
```
SETUP <<URL>> RTSP/1.0\r\n
CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n
User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Transport: <<VALUE>>\r\n
\r\n
```

## 4. PLAY
```
PLAY <<URL>> RTSP/1.0\r\n
CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n
User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Session: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Range: <<VALUE>>\r\n
\r\n
```

## 5. PAUSE
```
PAUSE <<URL>> RTSP/1.0\r\n
CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n
User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Session: <<VALUE>>\r\n
\r\n
```

## 6. TEARDOWN
```
TEARDOWN <<URL>> RTSP/1.0\r\n
CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n
User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Session: <<VALUE>>\r\n
\r\n
```

## 7. GET_PARAMETER
```
GET_PARAMETER <<URL>> RTSP/1.0\r\n
CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n
User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Session: <<VALUE>>\r\n
\r\n
```

## 8. SET_PARAMETER
```
SET_PARAMETER <<URL>> RTSP/1.0\r\n
CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n
User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Session: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Content-Type: <<VALUE>>\r\n
Content-Length: <<VALUE>>\r\n
\r\n
```

**Key Notes:**
- `<<URL>>` - typically the RTSP stream URL
- `CSeq` - increments with each request
- `Session` - obtained from SETUP response, required for PLAY/PAUSE/TEARDOWN
- `Transport` - specifies RTP profile (e.g., RTP/AVP/TCP or RTP/AVP/UDP)
- `Range` - playback time range (e.g., npt=0.0-10.0)
